Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:00:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Detect quote-removed builtin name subscript sinks

Normalize literal builtin name operands before arithmetic evaluation, preserve conditional escape semantics and data-only builtin options, and expose escaped names to the reference walk. Cache expansion boundaries across frames to retain linear scans. Proof: Bash 5.2.21 marker tests reproduce all 14 reported misses on main; original suite RED 24 failures/10 passes, expanded focused GREEN 167 tests. Existing quoted DATA lists unchanged.
